title: '[pallet-dap] Add genesis config for budget allocation'

doc:
  - audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
    description: |-
      `pallet-dap` gains a genesis configuration so the budget allocation can be seeded on a freshly
      initialised chain, keeping the DAP `try_state` invariants satisfied from block 0. The optional
      `budget_allocation` is validated exactly like `set_budget_allocation`: every key must be a
      registered `BudgetRecipient` and the parts must sum to 100%, otherwise genesis panics. When it
      is left `None`, a warning is logged and `BudgetAllocation` stays empty until governance calls
      `set_budget_allocation`.

      The previously disabled DAP `try_state` check is re-enabled behind a fixed `MIN_SEEDED_VERSION`
      floor of storage version v2: chains already upgraded by `MigrateV1ToV2`, and chains built from
      genesis, are verified, while older chains skip the check. No storage migration is introduced.

      The asset-hub-westend and staking-async parachain genesis presets, plus the asset-hub-westend
      emulated chain, seed the initial allocation with the same 15% DAP buffer / 85% staker rewards /
      0% validator incentive split that `MigrateV1ToV2` applied on existing chains, so fresh networks
      match already-running ones.

crates:
  - name: pallet-dap
    bump: minor
  - name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
    bump: patch
  - name: pallet-staking-async-parachain-runtime
    bump: patch
  - name: asset-hub-westend-emulated-chain
    bump: none
